[{:db/id "q-83574/selection/b3ec1657d2fca969c03f64975df0a057b163b62aab6d95ef615704c2e9a7679e" :answer/id #uuid "40969e71-1e1f-5c24-95f8-866f8add17b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83574/selection/23f22e6eaf8a74d947cddd27e829f88676674350961bdeead8aad751b93f7535" :answer/id #uuid "c515b014-53d0-58ee-ad42-badc30243574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83574/selection/b9c34ca4c2fd44941a940799983cd8b9c6c0f033fc95c671027bbd806aba22b8" :answer/id #uuid "abda21d8-36a7-5e38-9fce-6111e7e1eedd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83574/selection/c5b2cfd71d601ef44cc2b2e39376bc9ebd3a604f6738c2737906389d61e51f82" :answer/id #uuid "2c15f8ad-1048-5e50-9937-7b409e3d7041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83574/selection/5987df655cf650c678d879e1010692f15edeee5343968355f6a94eb4f6bcbf96" :answer/id #uuid "aad188e3-dc7f-56ed-95e3-3030b052d32b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83574/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74dc2061-4f07-51e4-a8b8-f2c3a9f1ef6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83574/selection/23f22e6eaf8a74d947cddd27e829f88676674350961bdeead8aad751b93f7535" :answer-field/choices ["q-83574/selection/b3ec1657d2fca969c03f64975df0a057b163b62aab6d95ef615704c2e9a7679e" "q-83574/selection/23f22e6eaf8a74d947cddd27e829f88676674350961bdeead8aad751b93f7535" "q-83574/selection/b9c34ca4c2fd44941a940799983cd8b9c6c0f033fc95c671027bbd806aba22b8" "q-83574/selection/c5b2cfd71d601ef44cc2b2e39376bc9ebd3a604f6738c2737906389d61e51f82" "q-83574/selection/5987df655cf650c678d879e1010692f15edeee5343968355f6a94eb4f6bcbf96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83574" :question/id #uuid "bd795f27-b6ec-5448-b236-dcfe908aea68" :question/math-academy-id "q-83574" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 14\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83574/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140472/selection/189c13ac93b327cac8d9b0acab13268b77736c7bb0b22d6c3e968f74f475c387" :answer/id #uuid "00287bb1-7e3c-56c5-bd02-121fa67b877f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140472/selection/0945aefcecfa337c4a7a0d61113c4685997c8a8fbf380364a902f5d3d8d60e56" :answer/id #uuid "04a5b74a-50ea-55b7-be9a-d53bc73a1686" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140472/selection/9a5ef0a06a852fbea671311347bf24f0c1a25057ec46187cc1db1414c6e0f45d" :answer/id #uuid "ef19a6d6-4434-52fb-ab98-6ceab6ab9c86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140472/selection/489eb8c38e24a51c8e397fe009adbca5674e0a274c57527bf5f070e876c4ac9b" :answer/id #uuid "de09d4be-8d92-5f4a-bd88-ac539e2ca901" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140472/selection/82c79a11c5f316588a4977bf9de059017422d38604e630b6407357df3b622d75" :answer/id #uuid "1f6fb764-6b5b-5040-9f8c-50374c9e41e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140472/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50551604-a11e-5a98-ab1c-a6bbadaa2c7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140472/selection/489eb8c38e24a51c8e397fe009adbca5674e0a274c57527bf5f070e876c4ac9b" :answer-field/choices ["q-140472/selection/189c13ac93b327cac8d9b0acab13268b77736c7bb0b22d6c3e968f74f475c387" "q-140472/selection/0945aefcecfa337c4a7a0d61113c4685997c8a8fbf380364a902f5d3d8d60e56" "q-140472/selection/9a5ef0a06a852fbea671311347bf24f0c1a25057ec46187cc1db1414c6e0f45d" "q-140472/selection/489eb8c38e24a51c8e397fe009adbca5674e0a274c57527bf5f070e876c4ac9b" "q-140472/selection/82c79a11c5f316588a4977bf9de059017422d38604e630b6407357df3b622d75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140472" :question/id #uuid "6d9b6de3-4396-5c82-b41c-2429c7a1964b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140472" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140472/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140472"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140473/selection/4d0f3d1792e5b538cea3a008af41f4567d058d2f553ffca031a47dcbfcabe7ca" :answer/id #uuid "da1e2779-04b4-5668-96b5-e5dc7e6153d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140473/selection/47718f5a96f0aa70f086bb1e4a91c14597a14d5b911e9ee255b066d72fb976c5" :answer/id #uuid "25f30edb-65c6-57e5-a87a-2942c767fb84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140473/selection/7a55afae4e9422f9a464974b2497d80b5f2b8a6766a9504e64a334d319284873" :answer/id #uuid "6b604f6b-e3cd-5806-9ab8-b1eebbe5ca81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140473/selection/7ac7d2959719e4bce5c22b340243de44bffc1f124fa341dd0452ee3afe8ca0b4" :answer/id #uuid "81378202-50c6-5cfb-9d56-d87add70a867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140473/selection/84604040d2292824dd3a6bd2e2ef7d12e8617580bd5b8a849da42baa0a656e65" :answer/id #uuid "7b1ad9e8-429b-5525-a1ec-ac537d61988f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140473/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5993fcab-56d3-5a1e-b900-f1a9dff0b051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140473/selection/7ac7d2959719e4bce5c22b340243de44bffc1f124fa341dd0452ee3afe8ca0b4" :answer-field/choices ["q-140473/selection/4d0f3d1792e5b538cea3a008af41f4567d058d2f553ffca031a47dcbfcabe7ca" "q-140473/selection/47718f5a96f0aa70f086bb1e4a91c14597a14d5b911e9ee255b066d72fb976c5" "q-140473/selection/7a55afae4e9422f9a464974b2497d80b5f2b8a6766a9504e64a334d319284873" "q-140473/selection/7ac7d2959719e4bce5c22b340243de44bffc1f124fa341dd0452ee3afe8ca0b4" "q-140473/selection/84604040d2292824dd3a6bd2e2ef7d12e8617580bd5b8a849da42baa0a656e65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140473" :question/id #uuid "8b3010e0-dd5b-598a-b59c-b5757e33b454" :question/math-academy-id "q-140473" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140473/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140473"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140474/selection/64921b7dd2da8f10acea44ef4c865de10b0ac7cff8ba81f2a9a44b79a745e085" :answer/id #uuid "37affad6-37a4-5a6b-a726-61e360cc673b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140474/selection/956d8eb35750c67db174a314ba4763f3c4674bb348dc8b3b766fbaf1a21a0df4" :answer/id #uuid "d22983a7-51c0-56b0-910c-ebbc06c54fda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140474/selection/57a2dbc018b6d7cf4cfb6095abba8d4dccd73c521d87e51730704ea86f47ee61" :answer/id #uuid "241d34f7-6b6f-5de6-a8d6-12a65a3952de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140474/selection/327b2796a63698a2f97f0b5c08c317b2d181e6af82d999b1293d92da244625a3" :answer/id #uuid "8921d29e-90ca-5250-bc27-9d64ca5ad81f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140474/selection/6a27def724e4439eb5e2dc21373e928503c9c05e4d4d0fa9ab62baba3e1daf66" :answer/id #uuid "2ce07f33-331e-5dd2-9a85-98167f4eafc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140474/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7724db94-374e-5532-a1f6-00d291074518" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140474/selection/57a2dbc018b6d7cf4cfb6095abba8d4dccd73c521d87e51730704ea86f47ee61" :answer-field/choices ["q-140474/selection/64921b7dd2da8f10acea44ef4c865de10b0ac7cff8ba81f2a9a44b79a745e085" "q-140474/selection/956d8eb35750c67db174a314ba4763f3c4674bb348dc8b3b766fbaf1a21a0df4" "q-140474/selection/57a2dbc018b6d7cf4cfb6095abba8d4dccd73c521d87e51730704ea86f47ee61" "q-140474/selection/327b2796a63698a2f97f0b5c08c317b2d181e6af82d999b1293d92da244625a3" "q-140474/selection/6a27def724e4439eb5e2dc21373e928503c9c05e4d4d0fa9ab62baba3e1daf66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140474" :question/id #uuid "2c94191a-43a1-5922-ab22-a6d441b65abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-140474" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 11\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{54}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140474/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140474"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158124/selection/80b70cbc61dccd2e57e6ea25179c5ed153ad9d29e784c51c8fe629635b68d2d8" :answer/id #uuid "cee3e6a6-60eb-5430-bda7-2d611d94d445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158124/selection/d5265175bfa835d404a63269c9d5a29facee3168c3c7ea1ad07418855b2207a4" :answer/id #uuid "1cd01e94-d2e8-5f5a-9530-ca5ddb6c3ffe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158124/selection/98243b419834507c07f3ab2b2bf5c8c31908e9eecebb05666ccf2f1709ce1741" :answer/id #uuid "0ea41735-e9e3-5b22-ac5a-ccde88cde448" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158124/selection/52f983c1e261e63eba86b7942f4547a0839137300af95672e2f7c0c445edd5a9" :answer/id #uuid "07e67ba4-c5bc-51b4-8b94-48e0b9249764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158124/selection/a51b5d98d135312d006e556f37cffdda39fee6cebfacdc46fdfba370ab35568c" :answer/id #uuid "cf4cb458-878d-55ac-80cb-d1daa8c12f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158124/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "71f9b5d5-cf31-5ef9-97f9-972e1c9edf6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158124/selection/52f983c1e261e63eba86b7942f4547a0839137300af95672e2f7c0c445edd5a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-158124/selection/80b70cbc61dccd2e57e6ea25179c5ed153ad9d29e784c51c8fe629635b68d2d8" "q-158124/selection/d5265175bfa835d404a63269c9d5a29facee3168c3c7ea1ad07418855b2207a4" "q-158124/selection/98243b419834507c07f3ab2b2bf5c8c31908e9eecebb05666ccf2f1709ce1741" "q-158124/selection/52f983c1e261e63eba86b7942f4547a0839137300af95672e2f7c0c445edd5a9" "q-158124/selection/a51b5d98d135312d006e556f37cffdda39fee6cebfacdc46fdfba370ab35568c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158124" :question/id #uuid "c81253d2-77a0-5506-9613-10f000472aac" :question/math-academy-id "q-158124" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}34 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{38}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 34\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158124/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158124"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
